  "id": "Fileless_Phantom_Stealer_Targets_Browser_Credentials_txt_8",
  "content": "Phantom Stealer's dropper is particularly notable because of its layered composition, which significantly hinders visibility into what the code is actually doing, says Aranzazu Mendez Casillas, a researcher with Fortra. \"What makes this specific case unique is how the dropper was composed,\" Casillas says in comments to Dark Reading. \"It wasn’t simply Base64, it was Base64 + XOR + donut. This means the attackers aren't focusing on the malware per se, but in the dropper, which means at the moment of analysis, researchers won't have a clear view of what's actually happening.\"",
  "category": "Article",
  "source": "Local Storage",
